WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:59.940
[Music]

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:06.860
[Narrator:] The time: the year 1881.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:15.740
The place: the General Hospital in the city of Vienna, Austria.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:26.080
Theodor Billroth, teacher of medicine, pioneer surgeon. 

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:36.760
The event:  so important that medical history records it as the beginning of a new era. 

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:45.379
The problem: to attempt a cure for a disease as old as humanity.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:53.420
[Music]

00:01:53.979 --> 00:02:00.979
The patient: Theresa Heller, admitted to the hospital four days ago. 

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:09.980
Symptoms: gastric pain for three months. Her diet, a few spoonfuls of sour milk daily.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:25.140
Pulse: thready. Evening temperature: 38.2 centigrade. Diagnosis: carcinoma of the pylorus.

00:02:29.569 --> 00:02:36.569
Up to this time, no malignant tumor of the
stomach had ever been successfully removed.

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:48.269
The hazards attending such an operation were
many. The ever- present threat of infection.

00:02:51.059 --> 00:02:58.959
The possibility of surgical shock. The dangers of prolonged anesthesia.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:07.180
The knowledge that others had failed.

00:03:09.209 --> 00:03:15.729
But pitted against this was Billroth's conviction that this was an early lesion, an operable case,

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:25.280
that his years of research could now be applied to the aid of a human being.

00:03:30.279 --> 00:03:37.359
Complete removal of the diseased tissue was the only way to prevent this patient's certain death.

00:03:45.299 --> 00:03:52.299
But removal of the cancer was not enough. A safe and adequate repair was of equal importance.

00:03:56.930 --> 00:04:03.930
As history now knows, this operation, the
Billroth I, was a success. 

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:12.380
More than any other fact, it proved the importance of early diagnosis followed by prompt, adequate treatment.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:30.600
Today, gastric cancer is still a serious medical
responsibility. Today, as in Billroth's day,

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:34.020
surgery offers to the patient the only hope
of cure.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:40.000
However, thanks to the great technical and
intellectual progress achieved in all branches

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:46.520
of medical science, the management of the
cancer patient is vastly improved.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:05:12.720
[Music]

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:21.980
The surgeon today, as did Billroth, intervenes in gastric cancer

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:25.680
in the hope that the disease is limited solely to the stomach.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:33.600
With this in mind, careful palpation of known sites of spread and of the stomach

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:39.580
determines the extent of the disease in these areas.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:48.960
Radical resection of the omentum together
with wide clearance of the lymph nodes

00:05:48.969 --> 00:05:53.909
is a routine measure to remove all possible disease.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:02.660
In the Billroth tradition, the pyloric tumor
can now be isolated by a safe margin

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:06.880
of the duodenal segment.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:14.960
Similarly, the major portion of the gastric
segment will be sacrificed.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:22.590
In most of the modifications of the Billroth
operation, the duodenum is closed and the

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:28.430
re-approximation of the remaining portion
of the stomach with the small intestine is established.

00:06:34.879 --> 00:06:40.569
The resultant anastomosis, tension-free and
airtight, will permit the patient normal dietary

00:06:40.569 --> 00:06:45.249
comfort with but slightly modified dietary
habit.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:52.240
Thus, the operation initiated by Billroth
more than 60 years ago remains today

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:57.760
the only treatment of gastric cancer that offers any
hope of cure.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:07.100
Of five major sites for malignant neoplasms, cancer of the stomach has the third highest incidence.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:14.580
However, of the mortality averages
for these sites, the mortality

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.700
of gastric cancer is among the highest.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:23.270
This disease causes more than one-fourth of
all cancer deaths. 

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:29.999
The reason for this high mortality is seen in the clinical behavior of cancer of the stomach.

00:07:29.999 --> 00:07:34.279
Although cancer may occur primarily in any area of the stomach, 

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:40.720
more than three-fourths of these lesions occur in the region of the pylorus. 

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.419
Dyspepsia or indigestion is the most common first complaint.

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:50.700
Here, as the cancer continues to grow, mechanical obstruction may take place.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:55.639
As a result of this growth, pain unrelated to food becomes evident.

00:07:55.639 --> 00:08:02.639
In addition, there may be loss of appetite,
vomiting, and fatigue. 

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.520
It is in this stage of disease, and because of these symptoms, 

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:10.080
that the average patient sees his physician.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.780
At the time of surgical exploration, often
delayed as much as several months,

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:21.180
the disease is usually found to have invaded the regional lymph nodes; 

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:28.381
however, one-third to one-half of all patients seen in this stage are still
candidates for resection.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:37.380
Nevertheless, despite radical resection, the tragic factor of delay permits local recurrence

00:08:37.409 --> 00:08:43.089
of disease, together with distant metastases, which result in the deaths 

00:08:43.089 --> 00:08:48.960
within five years of three-fourths of these patients.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:55.790
These deaths, added to all other gastric cancer deaths, account for the dark overall picture of gastric cancer.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:01.120
Any appreciable reduction
of this mortality requires that cancer be

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.940
suspected while it is still confined entirely
to the stomach.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:11.040
Unfortunately, this clinically young lesion
provides little evidence upon which to hang

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:16.880
this suspicion, either by the patient himself or by his physician.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:22.220
As a rule, the gastric cancer patient is a
mature adult with a complaint of vague dyspepsia,

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:26.940
whose tentative diagnosis is gastric ulcer.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:31.800
In other cases, the only early complaint may
be unexplained loss of weight

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:36.980
associated with some degree of secondary anemia.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:42.430
And sometimes the symptoms may not be suggestive
of gastrointestinal disease at all.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:52.170
In general, a mass is not palpable in early
gastric cancer. Although these symptoms -- chronic

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:57.860
dyspepsia with or without pain, anorexia,
weight loss, secondary anemia --

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:03.060
are suggestive of many disorders, the most
serious single disease, which may cause one

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:05.850
or any of them, is cancer.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:10.790
Therefore, whenever this suspicion exists,
the patient should be given the benefit of

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.690
a thorough examination.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:32.880
Early suspicion, accurate diagnosis, effective treatment.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:37.840
By application of this triad of management,

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.540
early stomach cancer can be excised sufficiently 

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:46.339
to reduce the likelihood of recurrence.

00:10:46.339 --> 00:10:52.479
The statistics in such cases of early gastric cancer show a mortality decrease of nearly half.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:05.220
A similar result can be achieved in breast
cancer. Of the four quadrants of the breast,

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:08.870
the upper outer quadrant is the usual site
of cancer.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:15.519
Regardless of site, however, the behavior
of breast cancer is quite uniform.

00:11:15.519 --> 00:11:21.230
In its early stage, this tumor, like most cancer, develops silently.

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:28.079
However, as growth continues, the connective
tissue is involved, resulting in flattening

00:11:28.079 --> 00:11:35.079
or dimpling of the skin. By the same process,
there is often retraction of the nipple.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:42.640
In addition, the regional nodes become involved because of lymphatic spread.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:49.940
It is at this stage of disease that the average patient is seen by her physician.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:57.660
The treatment permitting the greatest chance
for survival is a radical mastectomy.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:03.620
However, about three out of four patients so treated will succumb within five years,

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:10.630
due to a local recurrence and to distant metastases to the supraclavicular nodes,

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:18.100
the other breast, and to the lungs and bones.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:26.230
These cases, together with other breast cancer
fatalities, result in this statistical picture.

00:12:26.579 --> 00:12:31.579
Any reduction of this mortality requires that breast cancer be suspected

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:36.380
while it is confined entirely to the breast.

00:12:36.389 --> 00:12:43.389
The mass of early breast cancer, however, may be interpreted as benign disease.

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:51.340
Palpation alone is not enough to differentiate between a benign and a malignant mass.

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.960
Visualization of the breast in various positions
may be required 

00:12:55.970 --> 00:13:00.040
before eliciting a diagnostic sign of early cancer.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:09.340
This sign, skin retraction, so consistent
in malignancy, should call for an immediate

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:13.329
microscopic examination of suspected tissue.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:28.140
A local excision and examination of all breast tumors should be made in the operating room.

00:13:28.149 --> 00:13:35.149
If the excised mass is found to be malignant,
a radical mastectomy can be performed immediately.

00:13:40.899 --> 00:13:47.899
Except in rare cases, a simple mastectomy
has no place in the surgery of breast cancer.

00:13:50.129 --> 00:13:57.129
Adequate flap development permits better exposure of the operative field. 

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:06.860
This exposure makes possible thorough removal of both pectoral muscles.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:30.560
Removal of the pectoral muscles now permits meticulous dissection of the axilla.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:41.780
Only by such radical dissection, can suspected areas of spread be included

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:45.620
in the removal of the breast itself. 

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:51.960
In a great majority of cases following this operation, the patient will have the normal use of her arm.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:59.269
But what is vastly more important, the diseased
breast has been excised widely enough and

00:14:59.269 --> 00:15:04.909
and early enough to diminish the probability of recurrence. 

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:12.020
Thus, the mortality of early breast cancer can be effectively reduced.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:21.100
Cancer of the large bowel offers an equal
challenge,

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:25.560
inasmuch as nearly half of these growths occur in the rectum.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:33.220
Cancer of the rectum usually begins as a lesion confined to the mucosa.

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:41.880
As it grows, however, ulceration of the mucosa takes place, producing intermittent rectal bleeding.

00:15:41.889 --> 00:15:48.209
At the same time, mechanical venous blocking
may initiate hemorrhoids. 

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.840
A surprisingly large number of patients are treated for hemorrhoids 

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:59.460
without any investigation made to rule out the possibility of underlying cancer.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:04.970
As further growth of the tumor takes place, intraluminal obstruction produces constipation,

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:11.970
or diarrhea, or both alternately, with the stools frequently containing mucus and blood.

00:16:13.089 --> 00:16:20.609
It is with these symptoms and in this stage of disease that the patient generally sees his physician.

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:29.320
An abdominoperineal resection offers this patient the best opportunity for survival.

00:16:30.939 --> 00:16:36.300
But here again, the frequent delay of treatment
results in the recurrence of disease,

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:41.180
both locally and distantly, and accounts for the deaths within five years 

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:45.740
of more than three-quarters of these patients.

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:53.340
These losses from recurrence, together with cases considered inoperable,

00:16:53.480 --> 00:17:00.459
result in the high mortality of rectal cancer.

00:17:00.459 --> 00:17:05.430
Since more than half of rectal cancers originate
within reach of the examining finger,

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:12.430
here is the first and perhaps simplest line of attack against this disease.

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:22.410
If a rectal lesion is suspected or if rectal
symptoms are present, the patient should immediately

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:25.880
be given the benefit of a thorough examination.

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:31.640
This should, in addition to the digital examination,
include proctoscopy and x-ray, 

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:34.840
together with microscopic study of tissue specimens.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:49.230
In the treatment of rectal cancer, the rectum is first approached through an abdominal incision.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:52.450
This is necessary in order to free the lower bowel, 

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:57.280
a considerable segment of which must be included in the resection.

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:07.020
Here again, radical resection is a requirement in order to ensure the removal of all tissue

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:11.600
which may potentially be involved.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:26.350
The distal segment, after being carefully
capped to prevent contamination, is tucked

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:33.350
beneath the pelvic floor to be removed through
the perineum.

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:46.950
The proximal segment is carried through the
abdominal wall to form a colostomy.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:50.950
Patients may get along without soilage and even without a colostomy bag 

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:56.740
providing the bowel is irrigated thoroughly at regular intervals.

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:03.750
The perineal phase of the operation can usually
be undertaken immediately.

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:15.280
Careful dissection, much accomplished bluntly, prevents injury to the prostate and to the seminal vesicles.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:24.440
Extirpation of this disease is accomplished
by the complete removal of the rectum.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:29.400
By such adequate surgery, rectal cancer can be treated so as to reduce the likelihood of recurrence.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:37.120
The statistical picture of these early cases rewards our efforts

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:41.620
by showing a mortality decrease of dramatic proportions.

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:51.740
The female genital tract is a frequent site
of cancer and of these lesions,

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:56.880
about two-thirds occur in the cervix.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:03.670
In its early stage, this lesion may be misinterpreted
as a benign condition, such as cervical erosion.

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:10.670
As growth continues, however, leukorrhea usually
becomes evident or more pronounced, 

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:18.540
and with ulceration of the cervical mucosa, spotting or frank bleeding may occur.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:27.520
This bleeding in women of menopausal age is often mistakenly viewed as a sign of the change of life.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:31.620
Further extensive growth may take
place without new symptoms being added.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:36.440
Here again, we have a typical picture caused by delay, 

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:41.720
which too frequently the patient presents to her physician.

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:45.900
Radiation has been widely used in the treatment
of this disease. 

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:54.080
External radiation by high voltage x-ray, supplemented by intracavitary radium therapy, 

00:20:54.080 --> 00:21:01.080
has sufficient effect upon these lesions to permit the five-year survival of one out of four of these patients.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:07.080
Radiation therapy, however, is not the only form of treatment. 

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:12.680
Today, modern surgery together with improved pre- and postoperative care 

00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:18.120
permits complete extirpation of the disease with safety in selected cases.

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:28.900
In addition, the surgical approach allows visualization and the removal of the regional lymph nodes.

00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:38.500
Despite radical surgery, despite irradiation, most of these patients are seen too late,

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:47.280
and again, local recurrence of disease, lymphatic spread, and metastases cause the deaths

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:56.580
within five years of about three out of four, and so the average five-year result.

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:09.760
Cervical cancer must and can be suspected early. 

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:15.860
True, this lesion may be masked by leukoplakia or by cervical erosion.

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:20.880
Therefore, the family physician should take
advantage of tissue biopsy 

00:22:20.880 --> 00:22:27.260
in the presence of any cervical abnormality.

00:22:27.270 --> 00:22:32.430
Tissue biopsy is a diagnostic method of proved accuracy, 

00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:41.000
but on the other hand, a perfectly normal-appearing cervix may mask underlying early cancer.

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:45.980
To determine the likelihood of such occult
disease, 

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:53.000
the physician has at hand the cytologic method of cancer detection.

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:05.480
Such cytologic tests, followed by biopsy examinations, when indicated, 

00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:09.120
have an encouragingly high incidence of accuracy.

00:23:10.340 --> 00:23:16.120
A pelvic examination, including tissue or cytologic studies, should be made routinely

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:21.600
in all cases of vaginal complaint, if cervical cancer is to be found early.

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:25.140
And when such a routine study is found suspicious
of cancer, 

00:23:25.160 --> 00:23:29.540
the patient has the benefit of immediate treatment.

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:45.240
Effective treatment by irradiation often calls for massive x-ray dosage of the entire pelvis.

00:23:45.830 --> 00:23:52.030
This is frequently supplemented by the intracavitary
application of radium, or in some instances,

00:23:52.030 --> 00:23:55.540
radium may be the only form of therapy.

00:23:57.580 --> 00:24:01.840
Thus by adequate treatment, whether radiological or surgical, 

00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:09.260
cancer of the cervix can be interrupted early enough to minimize the danger of recurrence.

00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:16.660
The statistical picture of early cervical cancer shows a marked reduction in five-year mortality.

00:24:25.160 --> 00:24:31.700
In recent years, cancer of the lung has been diagnosed with increased frequency.

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:37.180
A major bronchus is the site of about four-fifths of all lung cancer. 

00:24:37.280 --> 00:24:44.980
The early growth of this tumor takes place by submucosal extension.

00:24:45.780 --> 00:24:50.680
At this stage, a preexisting cough becomes
aggravated. 

00:24:50.680 --> 00:24:57.720
Mucus becomes manifest and may well be stained with blood. 

00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:08.860
This cough is altogether too frequently interpreted by the patient or by his physician to be a cigarette cough or the result of a cold.

00:25:23.420 --> 00:25:28.380
Meanwhile, because of the delay, continued growth of the tumor, intraluminally,

00:25:28.560 --> 00:25:32.280
results in bronchial obstruction and resultant emphysema 

00:25:32.300 --> 00:25:37.200
or atelectasis with the likelihood of superimposed secondary infection.

00:25:37.200 --> 00:25:44.200
Extraluminally, the cancer invades the lung
peripherally and extends towards the pleura.

00:25:44.200 --> 00:25:50.910
This is the picture of disease which the average
patient presents at thoracotomy.

00:25:50.910 --> 00:25:55.970
About half of these patients, considered operable, are candidates for pneumonectomy;

00:25:55.970 --> 00:25:59.020
however, the delay is to be reckoned with 

00:25:59.020 --> 00:26:07.180
in metastases to lymph nodes such as peribronchial, paratracheal, 

00:26:07.740 --> 00:26:12.500
mediastinal, and abdominal,

00:26:13.040 --> 00:26:19.640
together with bloodborne spread to the other lung, to the bones, and other organs.

00:26:19.650 --> 00:26:25.230
Within five years, three-fourths of these
treated patients will be dead.

00:26:25.260 --> 00:26:32.540
Because of this insidious clinical behavior, lung cancer is one of our gravest cancer problems.

00:26:36.560 --> 00:26:39.980
Since early lung cancer provides little or
no sign of its presence,

00:26:39.980 --> 00:26:46.800
the detection of this disease by clinical means is one of the physician's most difficult tasks.

00:26:54.070 --> 00:26:58.290
On the other hand, a chest x-ray may provide a simple, effective method 

00:26:58.290 --> 00:27:03.930
of disclosing lung cancer in its earlier stages.

00:27:03.930 --> 00:27:08.470
Such an x-ray should be made on all cases with persistent cough.

00:27:08.480 --> 00:27:14.150
Nor should the history of a cold or a smoker's cough preclude the search for underlying cancer.

00:27:23.050 --> 00:27:30.070
In recent years, the advances of thoracic surgery have made thoracotomy a safe operative procedure.

00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:35.240
In some cases, this technique may be the only method of establishing the diagnosis.

00:27:51.810 --> 00:27:58.810
Careful palpation of the chest wall for evidence
of disease is the first step in exploration.

00:28:03.590 --> 00:28:08.590
If no extension is found and the tumor appears
to be confined entirely to the lung, 

00:28:08.590 --> 00:28:14.990
a pneumonectomy can offer this patient a good chance of survival.

00:28:23.150 --> 00:28:29.410
Closure of the bronchial stump is carried
out simultaneously with the amputation of the bronchus.

00:28:33.120 --> 00:28:40.120
Except in rare instances, lobectomy
has no place in the surgery of lung cancer.

00:28:45.310 --> 00:28:49.210
Only by total removal of the lung can cancer of this organ 

00:28:49.220 --> 00:28:53.560
be treated effectively enough to dim the danger of recurrence. 

00:28:53.660 --> 00:29:01.120
The benefit in such early management is fully worth the effort.

00:29:03.220 --> 00:29:09.660
Mortality of average cases, all cases, of
these five sites is high, 

00:29:09.680 --> 00:29:15.180
but in early cases, early suspicion, accurate diagnosis, and effective treatment 

00:29:15.260 --> 00:29:19.040
have brought about marked reductions in mortality.

00:29:19.860 --> 00:29:26.860
What is true of these five sites is equally
true of other sites of this disease.

00:29:32.630 --> 00:29:37.310
Our knowledge of cancer has grown tremendously in recent years 

00:29:37.310 --> 00:29:43.700
and the quest for additional knowledge is going on constantly in many fields of study.

00:29:43.710 --> 00:29:54.870
In chemotherapy, hormones, radioactivity,
carcinogenesis, virus research, genetics,

00:29:54.910 --> 00:29:58.730
and along numerous other avenues of approach.

00:29:58.730 --> 00:30:04.310
In one day to come, the results of this ever-increasing knowledge will lead us

00:30:04.360 --> 00:30:07.960
to the final answer to the cancer problem.

00:30:07.960 --> 00:30:14.320
However, the immediate problem, the cancer patient today,

00:30:14.380 --> 00:30:18.220
must be answered here and now,

00:30:18.220 --> 00:30:28.460
and by the man who has always borne the first responsibility for cancer detection, the family physician.

00:30:28.460 --> 00:30:55.760
[Music]

